      <section>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">This Privacy Policy explains how personal information relating to users located in South Africa is collected, used, disclosed, stored, and protected when you use the Chancen Companion mobile application (the “App”).</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">This Policy is issued in compliance with the Protection of Personal Information Act, 2013 (“POPIA”), applicable regulations, and guidance issued by the South African Information Regulator.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">This document supplements the Chancen Companion Master Privacy Policy. In the event of any conflict, this South Africa Privacy Policy Supplement shall prevail for users located in South Africa.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="about-the-app">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">1. About the Chancen Companion App</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">“Chancen Companion” refers to the mobile application operated by Chancen that allows users to access program information, including Income Share Agreement (ISA) participation details, communications, career resources, and financial literacy tools.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">The App supports students and graduates participating in Chancen education financing programs and related initiatives.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="responsible-party">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">2. Responsible Party</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">For users located in South Africa, the responsible party for purposes of POPIA is:</p>
        <div class="bg-secondary rounded-lg p-4 mb-3 text-sm text-subdued">
          <p class="font-semibold text-primary mb-1">Khanilor NPC t/a Chancen South Africa</p>
          <p>Registration Number: 2020/689306/08</p>
          <p>Registered Address: 676 Gallagher Avenue, Halfway House, Midrand</p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:companion@chancen.international" class="text-accent hover:underline">companion@chancen.international</a></p>
        </div>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">As the Responsible Party, Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd determines the purpose and means of processing personal information relating to users located in South Africa.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">The technical infrastructure supporting the App may be operated by Chancen International Services. Chancen International Services provides the technology platform and infrastructure that operates the App. However, Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd remains responsible for ensuring compliance with POPIA for users located in South Africa.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="information-regulator-registration">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">3. Information Regulator Registration</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">In accordance with POPIA, Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd has appointed an Information Officer responsible for overseeing compliance with POPIA and responding to privacy-related requests.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Information Officer contact details:<br>Email: <a href="mailto:edwin@chancen.international" class="text-accent hover:underline">edwin@chancen.international</a></p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">The Information Officer is registered with the South African Information Regulator where required by law.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="personal-information-collected">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">4. Personal Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">We may collect and process the following categories of personal data:</p>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Identity Information</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Full name</li><li>South African ID Number or student identification details</li><li>Date of birth (where required)</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Contact Information</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Email address</li><li>Phone Number</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Account Information</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Username and login credentials</li><li>Account activity within the App</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary mb-2">ISA Program Information</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>ISA participation status</li><li>Repayment obligations</li><li>Payment history</li><li>Balance estimates</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Device and Technical Information</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Device type</li><li>Operating system</li><li>IP Address</li><li>App usage data</li><li>Log information</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Communications Data</h3>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">When you contact support, provide feedback, or interact with the App’s AI chatbot, we may collect the information you share in those communications. This includes messages, questions, and responses exchanged with the chatbot.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">These interactions help us:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Respond to support requests</li><li>Improve the accuracy and usefulness of the chatbot</li><li>Improve our financial literacy tools</li><li>Enhance user experience and App functionality</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Where reasonably possible, we anonymise or de-identify information before using it for analytics, training, or product improvement purposes in order to protect user privacy.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">This may include:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Messages exchanged with Chancen through the App</li><li>AI chatbot interactions</li><li>Support requests</li><li>User feedback submissions</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Chancen collects only the personal information reasonably necessary to provide the App and support participation in Chancen programs.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="lawful-basis">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">5. Lawful Basis for Processing</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">We process personal information in accordance with POPIA and only where processing is justified, including on the following grounds:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Performance of a contract or taking steps linked to a contract</li><li>Compliance with legal or regulatory obligations</li><li>Legitimate interests of Chancen or the user</li><li>Protection of a legitimate interest of the data subject</li><li>Consent, where required by law</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Personal information is processed in a lawful and reasonable manner that does not unreasonably infringe the privacy of users.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="how-we-use-data">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">6. How We Use Personal Data</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Your personal data may be used for the following purposes:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Providing access to the Chancen Companion App</li><li>Displaying ISA participation and repayment information</li><li>Managing user accounts</li><li>Communicating program updates and notifications</li><li>Providing career, employment, and financial literacy resources</li><li>Maintaining platform security and preventing fraud</li><li>Improving App functionality and user experience</li><li>Complying with legal and regulatory obligations</li><li>Monitoring and improving AI chatbot performance</li></ul>
      </section>

      <section id="isa-account-data">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">7. ISA Account Data</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">The Chancen Companion App allows users to view information relating to their Income Share Agreement (ISA) participation.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">This may include:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Estimated ISA balance</li><li>Payment history</li><li>Repayment status</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">This information is derived from Chancen’s internal systems, including its Data Warehouse, which stores program and repayment information.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Balance information displayed in the App may not always reflect real-time updates and should be treated as an informational estimate only.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">The official record of ISA obligations is maintained by Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd. Users requiring official balance confirmations should contact Chancen directly.</p>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary mb-2">AI Chatbot and Automated Processing</h3>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">The Chancen Companion App may include AI-powered tools and chatbot functionality to assist users with financial literacy, support requests, and general informational queries.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">The chatbot may use automated processing to generate responses based on user inputs. However, important ISA-related decisions are not made solely through automated decision-making without appropriate safeguards.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Users have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Request human intervention</li><li>Request clarification regarding automated outputs</li><li>Challenge or correct inaccurate information generated by automated systems</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">These rights are provided in accordance with POPIA protections relating to automated decision-making.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="data-sharing">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">8. Data Sharing and Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Personal information may be shared with trusted third parties where necessary to operate the App and deliver Chancen services.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">These may include:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Cloud infrastructure providers</li><li>Technology service providers supporting the App</li><li>Payment processing partners (where applicable)</li><li>Legal or regulatory authorities where required by law</li><li>Analytics providers</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3"><strong>AI Technology Partners:</strong> We may use trusted technology providers, including AI service providers such as OpenAI, to process chatbot questions and generate responses.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Where reasonably practicable, we take steps to remove or mask directly identifying information before sharing data with these providers.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">We do not sell users’ personal information to third parties.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">All operators and service providers processing personal information on our behalf are required to implement appropriate confidentiality and security safeguards in accordance with POPIA.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="cross-border-transfers">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">9. Cross Border Transfers of Personal Information</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">To operate the Chancen Companion App, some personal information may be processed or stored outside South Africa.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">For example, technical infrastructure or support services may be provided by Chancen International Services in the United Kingdom or by international technology providers.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Where personal information is transferred outside South Africa, Chancen implements appropriate safeguards to ensure continued protection of personal information in accordance with POPIA.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">These safeguards may include:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Contractual data protection obligations with service providers and access controls</li><li>Secure cloud infrastructure and encryption</li><li>Technical and organizational security measures</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Cross-border transfers are conducted only where permitted under POPIA.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="data-security">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">10. Data Security</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Chancen takes appropriate, reasonable technical, and organisational measures to protect personal information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, disclosure, alteration and destruction.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Security measures may include:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Encryption of sensitive data</li><li>Restricted access controls</li><li>Secure infrastructure and monitoring systems</li><li>Internal policies governing data protection</li></ul>
      </section>

      <section id="data-retention">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">11. Data Retention</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Personal information is retained only for as long as necessary to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Provide App services</li><li>Support ISA program participation</li><li>Comply with legal accounting, or regulatory obligations</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Retention periods may vary depending on the nature of the data and applicable legal requirements.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Where users delete their App account through the App settings, Chancen will delete or de-identify App-related personal information within a reasonable period unless retention is required by law or necessary for legitimate business purposes.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="your-rights">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">12. Your Rights Under POPIA</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Under POPIA, users have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Be notified that personal information is being collected</li><li>Access personal information held about them</li><li>Request correction or updating of personal information</li><li>Request deletion or destruction of personal information where applicable</li><li>Object to certain types of processing</li><li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li><li>Object to direct marketing communications</li><li>Lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator</li><li>Institute civil proceedings in relation to unlawful processing</li><li>Not be subject to certain forms of solely automated decision-making</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Chancen respects these rights and has procedures in place to help users exercise them.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="exercising-your-rights">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">13. How to Exercise Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">To exercise your privacy rights, please contact Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd using the contact details provided below.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Requests should include sufficient information for us to verify your identity and locate the relevant personal information.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">We will respond within a reasonable time in accordance with POPIA requirements.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="complaints">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">14. Complaints</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">If you believe that Chancen has processed your personal information unlawfully or failed to protect your rights, you may submit a complaint to the South African Information Regulator.</p>
        <div class="bg-secondary rounded-lg p-4 mb-3 text-sm text-subdued">
          <p class="font-semibold text-primary mb-1">Information Regulator South Africa</p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:complaints.IR@justice.gov.za" class="text-accent hover:underline">complaints.IR@justice.gov.za</a></p>
          <p>Phone: <a href="tel:+27100235200" class="text-accent hover:underline">010 023 5200</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="policy-changes">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary mb-3">15. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Chancen may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 text-subdued space-y-1 mb-3"><li>Changes in legal or regulatory requirements</li><li>Changes in technology</li><li>Updates to App functionality</li><li>Operational changes</li></ul>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Updated versions will be made available within the App.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Continued use of the App after updates become effective constitutes acceptance of the revised Privacy Policy.</p>
        <p class="text-subdued mb-3">Where material changes are made, Chancen may provide additional notice through the App or via email.</p>
      </section>

